note: "Gate 0 green at the tip, re-run from a FORCED REBUILD. That caveat is the review's own finding rather than boilerplate: worktrees share target/debug/xtask and one target/, so cargo can judge a sibling's artifacts fresh and run them as yours - observed twice here, once with two neighbours' gates writing slots using this branch's xtask, once with cargo test running a stale binary that omitted four tests present in the source. Gate 0 can therefore report green for code it never compiled; its cached key is sound about the TREE and cannot see whose binaries ran. Recorded as a follow-up for the epic close, deliberately not fixed here - it is gate soundness rather than the cache, and widening this WU into it is the scope creep the epic's non-goals forbid. The final commit (904375e) is the result report's own record of rounds 3 and 4, a doc-only delta over the tip round 4 swept (bbc16b1); its factual claims were checked against the tip before it landed."
